===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|Caesar}}. Displaced {{cog|ang|cāsere}}, which would have yielded {{m|en||*caser}}, {{m|en||*coser}}, and {{cog|enm|keiser}}, {{m|enm|kaiser}}, from Old Norse and continental Germanic languages. All ultimately from the same Latin root. (See also {{m|en|Kaiser}} and {{m|en|tsar}}.)<ref>{{R:OED Online|code=26013}}</ref>

